From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Le Hoang Quyen <lehoangquyen@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:42:05 +0800
Subject: Metal: Handle non-OOM command buffer errors

Previously, ContextMtl::checkCommandBufferError() only raised an error
for MTLCommandBufferErrorOutOfMemory and silently discarded all other
MTLCommandBufferError codes (such as Timeout, PageFault, NotPermitted,
and DeviceRemoved), while ContextMtl::getResetStatus() unconditionally
returned NoError.

- Prevent AtomicCommandBufferError::store() from overwriting non-OOM
  GPU fault errors before they are popped.
- Handle non-OOM errors in ContextMtl::checkCommandBufferError() by
  setting mContextLost and raising an internal error.
- Return UnknownContextReset from ContextMtl::getResetStatus() when
  mContextLost is set.
- Check command buffer errors after GPU synchronization in
  FramebufferMtl::readPixelsImpl() and BufferMtl::mapRange().

Bug: chromium:568895029
Change-Id: I0e296243291b1bd698d2bc56ba715cab1c3ee3fa
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8542590
Commit-Queue: Quyen Le <lehoangquyen@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>

